## JSX Rules
1. Return Single Parent Element

Wrong:
return (
    <h1>Hello</h1>
    <p>React</p>
)

Correct:
return (
    <div>
        <h1>Hello</h1>
        <p>React</p>
    </div>
)

2. class becomes className

In JSX:

className="container"

instead of:

class="container"
Example
<div className="box">
    Welcome
</div>

3. JavaScript Inside JSX Uses Curly Braces

Example:

function App() {

    let name = "Sudarshan";

    return (
        <h1>Hello {name}</h1>
    );

}
JSX Gotchas

Gotchas means common mistakes/problems beginners make.

## Common JSX Gotchas
1. Multiple Parent Elements Not Allowed

Must wrap inside:

div
or
Fragment


2. class Keyword Cannot Be Used

Use:
className

3. Inline CSS Uses Object

Wrong:

<h1 style="color:red">

Correct:

<h1 style={{color:"red"}}>
Example
function App(){

    return(

        <h1 style={{color:"blue"}}>
            React Styling
        </h1>

    );

}

export default App;


4. Every JSX Tag Must Be Closed

Correct:

<img src="image.png" />
Simple React Example
File Name: App.js
